{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "Treat the 8 user stories as independent module migrations/ports from Spring XD to Spring Cloud Stream (s-c-s); each becomes a separate Gradle sub-module under the s-c-s repository.",
    "For 'move' user stories (U1–U6) the existing XD module code is largely copied and repackaged, with dependency updates and adaptation to the s-c-s channel binding API; for 'port' stories (U7, U8) deeper refactoring is required because the modules were originally not processor-style.",
    "Use Spring Cloud Stream's @EnableBinding / functional binding style to expose module inputs/outputs, replacing XD's Module-style adapters.",
    "Reuse Spring XD's existing module options metadata, translating them to s-c-s module configuration properties.",
    "Adopt Java 17 and Spring Framework 6.x as required by the project baseline.",
    "Test strategy combines JUnit 5 unit tests for option parsing/binding logic and Spring Cloud Stream integration tests using embedded test binders for end-to-end behavior.",
    "Common module packaging (jar layout, manifest, Spring auto-configuration registration) is implemented once and shared across the 8 modules via a parent pom/gradle script.",
    "Documentation is generated from a common template (README + option reference) reused for all 8 modules."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "The 'single developer' is experienced with both Spring XD internals and Spring Cloud Stream, so no ramp-up/training time is included.",
    "Source code of the original Spring XD modules is available and may be reused verbatim or with minimal changes for the 'move' stories.",
    "The literal token {{null}} in U2 refers to the actual Spring XD 'null' sink module (a module that simply consumes and discards messages); it is not a missing field.",
    "Each module already has well-defined behavior in XD, so the goal is functional equivalence in s-c-s, not redesign.",
    "No new infrastructure work (CI, repository creation, license headers) beyond what is needed to make the modules build and pass tests in the s-c-s repo.",
    "A 1 workday = 8 hours of focused development effort; estimates exclude meetings, code review turnaround time, and unrelated overhead.",
    "Integration testing uses embedded/in-memory brokers where possible (e.g., embedded MQTT broker, H2 for JDBC, mock HTTP server), so no external test infrastructure provisioning is required.",
    "Per-module effort includes code migration, unit tests, and one end-to-end integration test, but excludes long-running soak or performance tests."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "Project infrastructure and common setup",
      "activity_description": "Create the multi-module project layout in the s-c-s repo, configure the parent build (Gradle), set up shared dependency management, common auto-configuration plumbing for s-c-s modules, and a shared test harness base class."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "Migrate mqtt sink module (U1)",
      "activity_description": "Move the XD mqtt sink module into s-c-s: translate options, wire input channel binding, adapt MQTT client integration, write unit and integration tests using an embedded MQTT broker."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "Migrate null sink module (U2)",
      "activity_description": "Move the XD 'null' sink module into s-c-s: trivial consumer that discards incoming messages; implement binding, options, and basic tests."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "Migrate shell sink module (U3)",
      "activity_description": "Move the XD shell sink module into s-c-s: invoke external shell commands per incoming message; port ProcessBuilder logic, options, and tests."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "Migrate splunk sink module (U4)",
      "activity_description": "Move the XD splunk sink module into s-c-s: port HTTP-based Splunk HEC integration, options (host, token, index, etc.), and tests using a mock HTTP server."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "Migrate tcp sink module (U5)",
      "activity_description": "Move the XD tcp sink module into s-c-s: port TCP client/reactor-based connection handling, serialization options, and tests using a local embedded TCP server."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "Migrate jdbc source module (U6)",
      "activity_description": "Move the XD jdbc source module into s-c-s: port polling/JDBC query execution, row-mapping options, scheduled trigger, and tests using H2 with a populated schema."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8",
      "activity_name": "Port aggregator processor module (U7)",
      "activity_description": "Port the XD aggregator module into s-c-s as a processor: implement aggregation window, release strategies, correlation modes, options, and tests covering both time- and size-based windows."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A9",
      "activity_name": "Port http-client processor module (U8)",
      "activity_description": "Port the XD http-client module into s-c-s as a processor: implement request building, response handling, expected-response-status options, and tests using a mock HTTP server (MockWebServer)."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A10",
      "activity_name": "Cross-module integration testing",
      "activity_description": "Build and run an end-to-end streaming pipeline test that exercises representative modules together (e.g., jdbc source → aggregator → http-client processor → mqtt sink) to validate binding compatibility and message flow."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A11",
      "activity_name": "Documentation and release preparation",
      "activity_description": "Write per-module README and option reference using the shared template, update the s-c-s top-level documentation index, and prepare release notes / changelog entries for the 8 modules."
    }
  ],
  "most_likely_effort": {
    "A1": 2.0,
    "A2": 2.0,
    "A3": 1.0,
    "A4": 2.0,
    "A5": 2.0,
    "A6": 2.0,
    "A7": 3.0,
    "A8": 4.0,
    "A9": 3.0,
    "A10": 2.0,
    "A11": 1.5
  },
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 24.5
  }
}
```

